accTitle: Supply-chain request and simulation boundary
accDescr: A user request is interpreted and assessed by the agent. Planning proposes a typed candidate. A state-changing request passes through action capability and approval checks before the simulation-world adapter applies a command to the deterministic simulator. The simulator returns a new snapshot and effects, which can be observed by the agent.
flowchart TD
    User[User request] --> Agent[Agent application]
    Agent --> Evidence[Read modeled facts]
    Evidence --> Plan[Assess and propose recovery]
    Plan --> Candidate[Typed candidate action]
    Candidate --> Gate{Write action?}
    Gate -->|No| Report[Explain or request more evidence]
    Gate -->|Yes| Auth[Capability and approval checks]
    Auth --> World[Simulation-world adapter]
    World --> Sim[Deterministic simulator]
    Sim --> Result[New snapshot and typed effects]
    Result --> Observe[Versioned observation]
    Observe --> Agent
